 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "Each log is \"<timestamp>,<merchantId>,<statusCode>,<count>\" (logs may be unordered; records with the same key add up). Status 200 is success; every 4xx/5xx code is a distinct error. For each merchant, evaluation happens at each distinct timestamp t where it has records, over its records with t-windowSize+1 <= timestamp <= t. Alerts are strings \"<t>,<merchantId>,<statusCode>\" ordered by t, then merchant (code point), then code. Level 1: (merchant, code) alerts once, at the first evaluation where its error count in the window is >= threshold.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
